IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa8-helpers`

-- coa8-part15-records.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 15, Chapter 2 (accounting records), ss 386 to 389
-- (lines 4950-4995 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Two shapes of duty are encoded. A duty with a condition in its own words is encoded as "the company is required to ..." (JUST TRUE
-- where the duty applies; JUST FALSE where the text's own wording takes it away; NOTHING outside the wording). A duty that lists what
-- the records must contain is encoded as "the records ... as required" over the facts a witness can state. A duty whose "if" is unmet
-- imposes nothing, so the content check answers JUST TRUE for it (fork F3).

§ `Chapter 2: Accounting records`

-- ---- s 386: duty to keep accounting records ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4952 | (1) Every company must keep adequate accounting records.
@ref s 386(1) Duty to keep accounting records (src:4952)
GIVEN `s 1(1) the body is a company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386(1) the company is required to keep adequate accounting records` MEANS
    IF `s 1(1) the body is a company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every company must keep adequate accounting records"

-- src:4953 | (2) Adequate accounting records means records that are sufficient—
-- src:4954 | (a) to show and explain the company's transactions,
-- src:4955 | (b) to disclose with reasonable accuracy, at any time, the financial position of the company at that time, and
-- src:4956 | (c) to enable the directors to ensure that any accounts required to be prepared comply with the requirements of this Act ....
@ref s 386(2) Adequate accounting records (src:4953-4956)
GIVEN `sufficient to show and explain the company's transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sufficient to disclose with reasonable accuracy, at any time, the financial position of the company at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sufficient to enable the directors to ensure that any accounts required to be prepared comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386(2) the records are adequate accounting records` MEANS
    IF `sufficient to show and explain the company's transactions` AND `sufficient to disclose with reasonable accuracy, at any time, the financial position of the company at that time` AND `sufficient to enable the directors to ensure that any accounts required to be prepared comply with the requirements of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Adequate accounting records means records that are sufficient"

-- src:4957 | (3) Accounting records must, in particular, contain—
-- src:4958 | (a) entries from day to day of all sums of money received and expended by the company and the matters in respect of which the receipt and expenditure takes place, and
-- src:4959 | (b) a record of the assets and liabilities of the company.
@ref s 386(3) What the records must in particular contain (src:4957-4959)
GIVEN `entries from day to day of all sums of money received and expended by the company and the matters in respect of which the receipt and expenditure takes place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a record of the assets and liabilities of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386(3) the records contain what subsection (3) requires` MEANS
    IF `entries from day to day of all sums of money received and expended by the company and the matters in respect of which the receipt and expenditure takes place` AND `a record of the assets and liabilities of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Accounting records must, in particular, contain"

-- src:4960 | (4) If the company's business involves dealing in goods, the accounting records must contain—
@ref s 386(4) Where the business involves dealing in goods (src:4960)
GIVEN `the company's business involves dealing in goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386(4) the records are required to contain the stock and goods statements` MEANS
    IF `the company's business involves dealing in goods`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company's business involves dealing in goods"

-- src:4960 | (4) If the company's business involves dealing in goods, the accounting records must contain—
-- src:4961 | (a) statements of stock held by the company at the end of each financial year of the company,
-- src:4962 | (b) all statements of stocktakings from which any statement of stock as is mentioned in paragraph (a) has been or is to be prepared, and
-- src:4963 | (c) except in the case of goods sold by way of ordinary retail trade, statements of all goods sold and purchased, showing the goods and the buyers and sellers in sufficient detail to enable all these to be identified.
@ref s 386(4) The stock and goods statements (src:4960-4963)
GIVEN `the company's business involves dealing in goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `statements of stock held by the company at the end of each financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all statements of stocktakings from which any such statement of stock has been or is to be prepared` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every sale is of goods sold by way of ordinary retail trade` IS A BOOLEAN
      `statements of all goods sold and purchased show the goods and the buyers and sellers in sufficient detail to enable all these to be identified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386(4) the records contain the statements subsection (4) requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company's business involves dealing in goods`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text requires nothing where its "if" is unmet (fork F3)
    ELSE IF `statements of stock held by the company at the end of each financial year` AND `all statements of stocktakings from which any such statement of stock has been or is to be prepared` AND (`every sale is of goods sold by way of ordinary retail trade` OR `statements of all goods sold and purchased show the goods and the buyers and sellers in sufficient detail to enable all these to be identified`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the accounting records must contain— (a) statements of stock held by the company at the end of each financial year"

-- src:4964 | (5) A parent company that has a subsidiary undertaking in relation to which the above requirements do not apply must take reasonable steps to secure that the undertaking keeps such accounting records as to enable the directors of the parent company to ensure that any accounts required to be prepared under this Part comply with the requirements of this Act ....
@ref s 386(5) A parent company's duty as to a subsidiary undertaking's records (src:4964)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it has a subsidiary undertaking in relation to which the above requirements do not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386(5) the parent company is required to take reasonable steps to secure that the subsidiary undertaking keeps accounting records` MEANS
    IF `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `it has a subsidiary undertaking in relation to which the above requirements do not apply`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A parent company that has a subsidiary undertaking in relation to which the above requirements do not apply"

-- ---- s 387: duty to keep accounting records: offence ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4966 | (1) If a company fails to comply with any provision of section 386 (duty to keep accounting records), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 387(1) Offence: failure to comply with section 386 (src:4966)
GIVEN `s 386 the company fails to comply with a provision of section 386` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387(1) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with any provision of section 386 (duty to keep accounting records), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where an answer from section 386 or section 1121 is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 386 the company fails to comply with a provision of section 386` `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:4967 | (2) It is a defence for a person charged with such an offence to show that he acted honestly and that in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable.
@ref s 387(2) Defence: acted honestly and the default was excusable (src:4967)
GIVEN `the person acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387(2) this subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF `the person acted honestly` AND `in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence for a person charged with such an offence to show that he acted honestly and that in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable" (not shown: this subsection gives no defence on these facts, not "no defence at all")

-- src:4968 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:4969 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:4970 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:4971 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:4972 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 387(3) Penalties (src:4968-4972)
GIVEN conviction IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 387(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER conviction
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text distinguishes (i) England and Wales from (ii) Scotland or Northern Ireland

-- ---- s 388: where and for how long records to be kept ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4974 | (1) A company's accounting records—
-- src:4975 | (a) must be kept at its registered office or such other place as the directors think fit, and
-- src:4976 | (b) must at all times be open to inspection by the company's officers.
@ref s 388(1) Where the records are kept and who may inspect (src:4974-4976)
GIVEN `kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `kept at such other place as the directors think fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at all times open to inspection by the company's officers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(1) the accounting records are kept as subsection (1) requires` MEANS
    IF (`kept at the company's registered office` OR `kept at such other place as the directors think fit`) AND `at all times open to inspection by the company's officers`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company's accounting records— (a) must be kept at its registered office or such other place as the directors think fit, and (b) must at all times be open to inspection by the company's officers"

-- src:4977 | (2) If accounting records are kept at a place outside the United Kingdom, accounts and returns with respect to the business dealt with in the accounting records so kept must be sent to, and kept at, a place in the United Kingdom, and must at all times be open to such inspection.
@ref s 388(2) Records kept outside the United Kingdom (src:4977)
GIVEN `the accounting records are kept at a place outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `accounts and returns with respect to the business dealt with in those records are sent to, and kept at, a place in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those accounts and returns are at all times open to such inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(2) the accounts and returns for records kept outside the United Kingdom are kept as subsection (2) requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the accounting records are kept at a place outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text requires nothing where its "if" is unmet (fork F3)
    ELSE IF `accounts and returns with respect to the business dealt with in those records are sent to, and kept at, a place in the United Kingdom` AND `those accounts and returns are at all times open to such inspection`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "accounts and returns with respect to the business dealt with in the accounting records so kept must be sent to, and kept at, a place in the United Kingdom, and must at all times be open to such inspection"

-- src:4978 | (3) The accounts and returns to be sent to the United Kingdom must be such as to—
-- src:4979 | (a) disclose with reasonable accuracy the financial position of the business in question at intervals of not more than six months, and
-- src:4980 | (b) enable the directors to ensure that the accounts required to be prepared under this Part comply with the requirements of this Act ....
@ref s 388(3) What the accounts and returns must do (src:4978-4980)
GIVEN `the accounting records are kept at a place outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longest interval between the dates at which the accounts and returns disclose the financial position of the business, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `they disclose it with reasonable accuracy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they enable the directors to ensure that the accounts required to be prepared under this Part comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(3) the accounts and returns sent to the United Kingdom are such as subsection (3) requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the accounting records are kept at a place outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text requires nothing where its "if" is unmet (fork F3)
    ELSE IF `the longest interval between the dates at which the accounts and returns disclose the financial position of the business, in months` AT MOST 6 AND `they disclose it with reasonable accuracy` AND `they enable the directors to ensure that the accounts required to be prepared under this Part comply with the requirements of this Act`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be such as to— (a) disclose with reasonable accuracy the financial position of the business in question at intervals of not more than six months"

-- src:4984 | (5) Subsection (4) is subject to any provision contained in rules made under section 411 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) (company insolvency rules) or Article 359 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 388(5) Subsection (4) is subject to insolvency rules (src:4984)
-- The rules (section 411 of the Insolvency Act 1986, Article 359 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989) are not among the sources:
-- whether one of their provisions applies is a borrowed fact, passed through.
GIVEN `a provision of rules made under section 411 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 359 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(5) a provision of insolvency rules displaces subsection (4)` MEANS
    `a provision of rules made under section 411 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 359 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 applies`

-- src:4981 | (4) Accounting records that a company is required by section 386 to keep must be preserved by it—
-- src:4982 | (a) in the case of a private company, for three years from the date on which they are made;
-- src:4983 | (b) in the case of a public company, for six years from the date on which they are made.
@ref s 388(4) How long the records must be preserved (src:4981-4983)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Period
`s 388(4) the period for which the accounting records must be preserved` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    THEN Period OF 6, Years
    ELSE Period OF 3, Years

-- "for three years from the date on which they are made" (six for a public company): the text does not say whether the anniversary
-- day itself is within the period (the Interpretation Act 1978 is not among the sources), so that day answers NOTHING.
-- src:4981 | (4) Accounting records that a company is required by section 386 to keep must be preserved by it—
-- src:4982 | (a) in the case of a private company, for three years from the date on which they are made;
-- src:4983 | (b) in the case of a public company, for six years from the date on which they are made.
@ref s 388(4) How long the records must be preserved (src:4981-4983)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the records were made` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
      `s 388(5) a provision of insolvency rules displaces subsection (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(4) the accounting records must still be preserved on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 388(5) a provision of insolvency rules displaces subsection (4)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a provision of the insolvency rules applies is not known
    WHEN JUST displaced THEN
        IF displaced
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any provision contained in rules made under section 411 of the Insolvency Act 1986"
        ELSE IF day LESS THAN anniversary
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE IF day EQUALS anniversary
                  THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the anniversary day is inside "for three years from the date on which they are made"
                  ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a private company, for three years from the date on which they are made; (b) in the case of a public company, for six years from the date on which they are made"
    WHERE
        anniversary MEANS `add years` `the date on which the records were made` (IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` THEN 6 ELSE 3)

-- ---- s 389: where and for how long records to be kept: offences -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4986 | (1) If a company fails to comply with any provision of subsections (1) to (3) of section 388 (requirements as to keeping of accounting records), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 389(1) Offence: failure to comply with section 388(1) to (3) (src:4986)
GIVEN `s 388 the company fails to comply with a provision of subsections (1) to (3) of section 388` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(1) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with any provision of subsections (1) to (3) of section 388 (requirements as to keeping of accounting records), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where an answer from section 388 or section 1121 is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 388 the company fails to comply with a provision of subsections (1) to (3) of section 388` `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:4987 | (2) It is a defence for a person charged with such an offence to show that he acted honestly and that in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable.
@ref s 389(2) Defence: acted honestly and the default was excusable (src:4987)
GIVEN `the person acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(2) this subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF `the person acted honestly` AND `in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence for a person charged with such an offence to show that he acted honestly and that in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable" (not shown: this subsection gives no defence on these facts)

-- src:4988 | (3) An officer of a company commits an offence if he—
-- src:4989 | (a) fails to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance by the company with subsection (4) of that section (period for which records to be preserved), or
-- src:4990 | (b) intentionally causes any default by the company under that subsection.
@ref s 389(3) Offence: the preservation period (src:4988-4990)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `fails to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance by the company with subsection (4) of that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `intentionally causes any default by the company under that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(3) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer of the company` AND (`fails to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance by the company with subsection (4) of that section` OR `intentionally causes any default by the company under that subsection`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An officer of a company commits an offence if he— (a) fails to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance by the company with subsection (4) of that section (period for which records to be preserved), or (b) intentionally causes any default by the company under that subsection"

-- src:4991 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:4992 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:4993 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:4994 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:4995 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 389(4) Penalties (src:4991-4995)
GIVEN conviction IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 389(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    `s 387(3) the penalty on conviction` conviction
